-- #845 SECOND SHAPE, found by adversarial review of the first fix (#1114): the callee is
-- reached through an `export import` RE-EXPORT rather than named directly.
--
-- ⚠️ THE CORPUS HAD NO RE-EXPORT FIXTURE AT ALL before this one — 132 files, zero — and
-- that absence is why the gap shipped. It is not a novel shape: it is the recurrence
-- `.claude/workstreams/TYPECHECK.md` records for #1283 ("the decl's origin names the
-- declaring module and the import path names the re-exporter, so the identity test
-- misses") and that `renameAliasedMethods` already learned for the METHOD tables. A
-- cross-module keying fix that is not exercised through a re-export has tested the easy
-- half of its own rule.
--
-- Before the fix: `check` **0**, `run` `unknown op '+'`, `build` **0 with a binary
-- written**, and that binary **segfaulted (139)** — verbatim #845, one hop out. The
-- discriminator was decisive and it favoured the first fix: the same callee imported
-- DIRECTLY (reject_845_xmod_inferred_selective.mdk) already rejected correctly.
import lib.obl1114_reexp.{f}

main = println (f "abc")
